{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PsBVH4txQAzKUpdwEGX4Xz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Atomic recipes\n2\t\n3\t`taskspec recipe list` discovers pinned strategies. `recipe show <strategy>` emits\n4\ta resolved example; `recipe validate <file> --budget <n>` validates a resolved\n5\trecipe. TaskPlan units accept either a strategy name or a resolved recipe mapping.\n6\tNative authored decomposition recipes accept strategy names.\n7\t\n8\tStrategies are direct, plan-execute-verify, diagnose-repair-verify, test-first, and\n9\tresearch-synthesize-verify. Their guidance resolves into the Validation Card's\n10\tagent contract before HMAC authorization. Changing installed strategy instructions\n11\tcannot alter a sealed task. Use relevant context, examples when needed, tool\n12\tfeedback, explicit deliverables, and concise self-checks; do not request private\n13\treasoning transcripts.\n14\t\n15\tEach recipe stays within one outcome, scope, authority, and timeout. Internal\n16\tsteps are sequential. Independent ownership or acceptance requires another leaf.\n17\tNew recipes default to three executor-plus-evaluation rounds and stop after two\n18\tidentical failing-eval/write-digest observations, capped by the signed budget.\n19\tTimeout and consumed rounds persist across replacement attempts of the same\n20\trevision. Cancellation, stale authorization, scope escape, and unavailable required\n21\tenforcement stop work. Optional usage metrics remain null when unavailable.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abf1529-dfad-44b4-923a-1389e8368909","uuid":"8adc65f9-e14e-4594-abba-1f99e6df58a0","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:50:47.253Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/recipes.md","content":"# Atomic recipes\n\n`taskspec recipe list` discovers pinned strategies. `recipe show <strategy>` emits\na resolved example; `recipe validate <file> --budget <n>` validates a resolved\nrecipe. TaskPlan units accept either a strategy name or a resolved recipe mapping.\nNative authored decomposition recipes accept strategy names.\n\nStrategies are direct, plan-execute-verify, diagnose-repair-verify, test-first, and\nresearch-synthesize-verify. Their guidance resolves into the Validation Card's\nagent contract before HMAC authorization. Changing installed strategy instructions\ncannot alter a sealed task. Use relevant context, examples when needed, tool\nfeedback, explicit deliverables, and concise self-checks; do not request private\nreasoning transcripts.\n\nEach recipe stays within one outcome, scope, authority, and timeout. Internal\nsteps are sequential. Independent ownership or acceptance requires another leaf.\nNew recipes default to three executor-plus-evaluation rounds and stop after two\nidentical failing-eval/write-digest observations, capped by the signed budget.\nTimeout and consumed rounds persist across replacement attempts of the same\nrevision. Cancellation, stale authorization, scope escape, and unavailable required\nenforcement stop work. Optional usage metrics remain null when unavailable.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf455vXrb6Ppoi7QifLJT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YF6fMzozJfjBhpL6jG8Xib","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13098,"cache_read_input_tokens":17406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13098},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abf1529-dfad-44b4-923a-1389e8368909","uuid":"54404859-e5cd-4d63-a35b-c69a6f999d13","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:50:48.113Z","request_id":"req_011Cf455uxsUMbfHVFRkQX93","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YF6fMzozJfjBhpL6jG8Xib":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YF6fMzozJfjBhpL6jG8Xib","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# First accepted task and evidence\n2\t\n3\tFor one small understood change, author `TaskPlan/v1`, preview it with\n4\t`taskspec plan --manifest <file>`, and materialize with `taskspec batch --plan <file>`.\n5\tInspect `taskspec validate <spec>`, `taskspec dod <spec>`, and every eval. An eval\n6\tmust discriminate a real result from a stub; metadata compliance is not behavioral proof.\n7\t\n8\tRecord human authorization with `taskspec gate --stamp <spec> --stamp-by <identity>`.\n9\tFor ordinary tasks, create an attempt handoff using\n10\t`taskspec handoff <spec> --backend <backend> --out <path>`, execute within it, and\n11\tuse canonical `taskspec accept --handoff <path> --stamp <spec>` with the required\n12\treceipts and supervisor decision. For managed recipes use the Mesh route in the\n13\texecution guide. Failed evals, stale revisions, and missing required attestations\n14\tcannot establish acceptance. Never edit sealed evals to make work pass.\n15\t\n16\t`taskspec status --initiative <id>` reconstructs acceptance from canonical records,\n17\tseparately from lifecycle status. `graph --initiative <id> --view capabilities`\n18\tshows explicit integration proof gaps. Passing child tasks does not prove a capability,\n19\ta successful pipeline does not establish service health, and acceptance does not\n20\tauthorize production release.\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abf1529-dfad-44b4-923a-1389e8368909","uuid":"8d0fe8f0-2842-4aa2-9af4-4a300875724f","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:50:48.121Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md","content":"# First accepted task and evidence\n\nFor one small understood change, author `TaskPlan/v1`, preview it with\n`taskspec plan --manifest <file>`, and materialize with `taskspec batch --plan <file>`.\nInspect `taskspec validate <spec>`, `taskspec dod <spec>`, and every eval. An eval\nmust discriminate a real result from a stub; metadata compliance is not behavioral proof.\n\nRecord human authorization with `taskspec gate --stamp <spec> --stamp-by <identity>`.\nFor ordinary tasks, create an attempt handoff using\n`taskspec handoff <spec> --backend <backend> --out <path>`, execute within it, and\nuse canonical `taskspec accept --handoff <path> --stamp <spec>` with the required\nreceipts and supervisor decision. For managed recipes use the Mesh route in the\nexecution guide. Failed evals, stale revisions, and missing required attestations\ncannot establish acceptance. Never edit sealed evals to make work pass.\n\n`taskspec status --initiative <id>` reconstructs acceptance from canonical records,\nseparately from lifecycle status. `graph --initiative <id> --view capabilities`\nshows explicit integration proof gaps. Passing child tasks does not prove a capability,\na successful pipeline does not establish service health, and acceptance does not\nauthorize production release.\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
