{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf45FDbX6VchmHvq8ddZm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BzEkoCFMpwW1jKzn8BLWAX","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/tasks/.plans/rate-limit-policy-schema.yaml","old_string":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n                     \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","new_string":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\", \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":46384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abf1529-dfad-44b4-923a-1389e8368909","uuid":"5b9e8cad-c6f2-4120-8704-a9f814b5587a","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:52:56.885Z","request_id":"req_011Cf45FD8jzXgHa8ETCTa6H","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BzEkoCFMpwW1jKzn8BLWAX":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/tasks/.plans/rate-limit-policy-schema.yaml","old_string":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n                     \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","new_string":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\", \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzEkoCFMpwW1jKzn8BLWAX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/tasks/.plans/rate-limit-policy-schema.yaml has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abf1529-dfad-44b4-923a-1389e8368909","uuid":"ba63f5df-951b-4ee7-a352-de8c45092ce1","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:52:56.897Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat iw54pyk7/tasks/.plans/rate-limit-policy-schema.yaml","oldString":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n                     \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","newString":"              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\", \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","originalFile":"api_version: taskspec.dev/v1\nkind: TaskPlan\napproved: false\nmetadata:\n  name: rate-limit-policy-schema\n  source: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\nunits:\n  - id: T-20260914-rate-limit-policy-schema\n    title: Add a versioned rate-limit policy schema that rejects invalid limits and windows\n    effort: S\n    profile: standard\n    agent: any\n    execution_backend: any\n    depends_on: []\n    touches_paths: []\n    creates_paths:\n      - src/policy/__init__.py\n      - src/policy/schema.py\n      - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n    source_note: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    why: >-\n      Step 1 of the rate-limiting steel thread. Every later step (resolution,\n      denial, telemetry) reads a policy document, so a malformed limit or window\n      accepted here becomes a wrong allow/deny decision later with no local\n      signal. Validation has to fail at the schema boundary, and the boundary has\n      to be versioned so a future policy shape is a named rejection rather than a\n      silent reinterpretation of old fields.\n    goal: >-\n      Add a stdlib-only policy schema module that parses one rate-limit policy\n      document, returns a normalized policy for a supported schema version, and\n      rejects unsupported versions, out-of-domain limits, and out-of-domain\n      windows with stable machine-readable error codes.\n    done_condition: >-\n      validate_policy accepts a well-formed supported-version document and\n      rejects every declared invalid limit, window, and schema version with the\n      declared error code and field, proven by the evals in this spec.\n    context: >-\n      Greenfield: this repository has no application source yet, so the atom\n      creates its own module and tests. Assumptions made at authoring time, open\n      to change in review: Python 3 stdlib only (no YAML/JSON-schema dependency,\n      so evals run offline); the policy document is a plain dict; the accepted\n      domain is limit as an int in 1..1000000 and window_seconds as an int in\n      1..86400; bool is not an acceptable int; numeric strings are not coerced;\n      supported schema versions are exactly (\"1.0\",) and schema_version is\n      required with no default. The 100-requests-per-window figure in the\n      blueprint is policy data, not a schema constant.\n    behaviors:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a policy document whose schema_version is supported and whose limit and window are in domain\n        when: validate_policy is called with it\n        then: it returns a normalized policy exposing schema_version, org_id, limit, and window_seconds\n      - id: B-2\n        given: a policy document whose limit is not an int in 1..1000000, including bool and numeric strings\n        when: validate_policy is called with it\n        then: it raises PolicySchemaError with code \"invalid_limit\" and field \"limit\"\n      - id: B-3\n        given: a policy document whose window_seconds is not an int in 1..86400, including bool and numeric strings\n        when: validate_policy is called with it\n        then: it raises PolicySchemaError with code \"invalid_window\" and field \"window_seconds\"\n      - id: B-4\n        given: a policy document whose schema_version is missing, empty, or outside the supported set\n        when: validate_policy is called with it\n        then: it raises PolicySchemaError with code \"unsupported_schema_version\" and field \"schema_version\", without defaulting to the current version\n    evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: a supported-version document with an in-domain limit and window normalizes\n        command: |\n          PYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PY'\n          from policy.schema import validate_policy\n          p = validate_policy({\n              \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n              \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n              \"limit\": 100,\n              \"window_seconds\": 60,\n          })\n          assert p.schema_version == \"1.0\", p\n          assert p.org_id == \"org-123\", p\n          assert p.limit == 100, p\n          assert p.window_seconds == 60, p\n          PY\n        verifies:\n          - B-1\n        expected_duration_sec: 10\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: every out-of-domain limit is rejected with code invalid_limit on field limit\n        command: |\n          PYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PY'\n          from policy.schema import PolicySchemaError, validate_policy\n          bad = [0, -1, 1000001, True, False, \"100\", 1.5, None]\n          for value in bad:\n              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n                     \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}\n              try:\n                  validate_policy(doc)\n              except PolicySchemaError as err:\n                  assert err.code == \"invalid_limit\", (value, err.code)\n                  assert err.field == \"limit\", (value, err.field)\n              else:\n                  raise AssertionError(\"accepted invalid limit: %r\" % (value,))\n          PY\n        verifies:\n          - B-2\n        expected_duration_sec: 10\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: every out-of-domain window is rejected with code invalid_window on field window_seconds\n        command: |\n          PYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PY'\n          from policy.schema import PolicySchemaError, validate_policy\n          bad = [0, -60, 86401, True, False, \"60\", 60.5, None]\n          for value in bad:\n              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",\n                     \"limit\": 100, \"window_seconds\": value}\n              try:\n                  validate_policy(doc)\n              except PolicySchemaError as err:\n                  assert err.code == \"invalid_window\", (value, err.code)\n                  assert err.field == \"window_seconds\", (value, err.field)\n              else:\n                  raise AssertionError(\"accepted invalid window: %r\" % (value,))\n          PY\n        verifies:\n          - B-3\n        expected_duration_sec: 10\n      - id: eval_4\n        description: missing, empty, and unsupported schema versions are rejected instead of defaulted\n        command: |\n          PYTHONPATH=src python3 - <<'PY'\n          from policy.schema import SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS, PolicySchemaError, validate_policy\n          assert tuple(SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS) == (\"1.0\",), SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS\n          base = {\"org_id\": \"org-123\", \"limit\": 100, \"window_seconds\": 60}\n          for value in [\"\", \"0.9\", \"2.0\", \"1\", 1.0, None, \"__MISSING__\"]:\n              doc = dict(base)\n              if value != \"__MISSING__\":\n                  doc[\"schema_version\"] = value\n              try:\n                  validate_policy(doc)\n              except PolicySchemaError as err:\n                  assert err.code == \"unsupported_schema_version\", (value, err.code)\n                  assert err.field == \"schema_version\", (value, err.field)\n              else:\n                  raise AssertionError(\"accepted schema version: %r\" % (value,))\n          PY\n        verifies:\n          - B-4\n        expected_duration_sec: 10\n      - id: eval_5\n        description: the module's own unit tests exist and pass\n        command: |\n          PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_policy_schema*.py' -v\n        verifies:\n          - B-1\n          - B-2\n          - B-3\n          - B-4\n        terminal: true\n        expected_duration_sec: 30\n    anti_patterns:\n      - Do not default an absent or empty schema_version to the current version; an unversioned document is a rejection, not a guess.\n      - Do not accept bool as an int limit or window; isinstance(True, int) is True in Python and must be excluded explicitly.\n      - Do not coerce numeric strings or floats into ints; \"100\" and 1.5 are rejections, not inputs to int().\n      - Do not raise bare ValueError or return a bool; callers in later steel-thread steps branch on the stable code and field.\n      - Do not add a YAML, pydantic, or jsonschema dependency; evals must run offline against the stdlib.\n      - Do not widen into policy resolution, request counting, denial, or telemetry; those are separate steel-thread steps.\n    do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      - .taskspec/\n      - .agents/\n      - .claude/\n      - tasks/\n    rollback: >-\n      Delete src/policy/ and tests/test_policy_schema.py. Nothing else in the\n      repository imports them, so removal restores the prior state exactly.\n    observability: >-\n      (none) — this atom is a pure validation boundary with no runtime emission.\n      Decision telemetry is step 4 of the steel thread.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":88,"oldLines":8,"newStart":88,"newLines":7,"lines":["           from policy.schema import PolicySchemaError, validate_policy","           bad = [0, -1, 1000001, True, False, \"100\", 1.5, None]","           for value in bad:","-              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\",","-                     \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","+              doc = {\"schema_version\": \"1.0\", \"org_id\": \"org-123\", \"limit\": value, \"window_seconds\": 60}","               try:","                   validate_policy(doc)","               except PolicySchemaError as err:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
